# tapps-brain

Persistent cross-session memory system for AI coding assistants. Fully deterministic (no LLM calls), **PostgreSQL-only** persistence (private memory, Hive, Federation), pgvector HNSW + tsvector hybrid retrieval, BM25 ranking, exponential decay, automatic consolidation, cross-project federation.

## Build & Development Commands

```bash
# Install dependencies (uses uv package manager)
uv sync --group dev

# Optional extras (see pyproject.toml): cli, mcp, reranker, otel, visual, all

# Run all tests (CI-style: exclude benchmarks)
pytest tests/ -v --tb=short -m "not benchmark" --cov=tapps_brain --cov-report=term-missing --cov-fail-under=95

# Production release gate (packaging, version tests, pytest, ruff, mypy)
# Linux / macOS / WSL or Git Bash: bash scripts/release-ready.sh

# Run a single test file
pytest tests/unit/test_memory_store.py -v

# Lint
ruff check src/ tests/

# Format check
ruff format --check src/ tests/

# Auto-fix lint/format
ruff check --fix src/ tests/
ruff format src/ tests/

# Type check (strict mode)
mypy --strict src/tapps_brain/
```

## Architecture

**Implementation baseline** — `docs/engineering/` (ground-truth architecture, flows, schema, optional paths).

### Source layout: `src/tapps_brain/`

**Storage layer** — `store.py` is the main `MemoryStore` class: in-memory dict + Postgres write-through, thread-safe via `threading.Lock`. Per-agent isolation via `(project_id, agent_id)` on every private row (EPIC-053). `health()` returns `StoreHealthReport` (includes `profile_seed_version` when `profile.seeding.seed_version` is set). `postgres_private.py` handles the private memory backend; schema migrations live in `src/tapps_brain/migrations/private/` (currently v1–027; max version **027** = `memory_status`, renumbered from the historical 015 collision). MCP tool/resource counts: `docs/generated/mcp-tools-manifest.json`. See `docs/planning/STATUS.md` for a release snapshot.

**Data model** — `models.py` defines `MemoryEntry` (Pydantic v2) with tier-based classification (`MemoryTier`: architectural/pattern/procedural/context), source tracking, scope visibility, and access counting.

**Retrieval** — `retrieval.py` uses composite scoring: relevance 40%, confidence 30%, recency 15%, frequency 15% with the default `repo-brain` profile (no-profile code fallback: frequency 10% + graph centrality 5%). `bm25.py` provides BM25 (BM25+ variant). `fusion.py` implements Reciprocal Rank Fusion for hybrid search. Optional `profile.hybrid_fusion` (`HybridFusionConfig`) tunes per-channel top-k and RRF *k*; used by `inject_memories` → `MemoryRetriever`.

**Memory lifecycle** — `decay.py` applies exponential decay with tier-specific half-lives. `consolidation.py` + `auto_consolidation.py` merge memories deterministically using Jaccard + TF-IDF similarity (no LLM). `gc.py` archives stale memories to Postgres `gc_archive` (dry-run + metrics, EPIC-044.5). Max-entry eviction: `docs/engineering/data-stores-and-schema.md` (optional `limits.max_entries_per_group`, STORY-044.7). `evaluation.run_consolidation_threshold_sweep` + CLI `maintenance consolidation-threshold-sweep`; merge undo `MemoryStore.undo_consolidation_merge` + CLI `maintenance consolidation-merge-undo` (EPIC-044.4). `MemoryProfile.seeding.seed_version` → `profile_seed_version` on health/stats (EPIC-044.6).

**Safety** — `safety.py` detects prompt injection patterns and sanitizes/blocks RAG content.

**Federation** — `postgres_federation.py` enables cross-project memory sharing via PostgreSQL (`TAPPS_BRAIN_FEDERATION_DSN`).

### Key design decisions

- **Postgres-only persistence** (ADR-007) — no SQLite or in-process fallback
- **Synchronous by design** — no async/await in core code
- **Write-through cache** — all mutations update both in-memory dict and Postgres
- **Lazy decay** — exponential decay computed on read, not via background tasks
- **Deterministic merging** — consolidation uses similarity thresholds, never LLM calls
- **Max 5,000 entries per project** (default; profile-configurable) — enforced in MemoryStore

