## Local Docker deploy (agents)

When upgrading tapps-brain on the **local unified stack** (`docker-compose.hive.yaml`, project `tapps-brain`):

| Situation | Command |
|---|---|
| First-time | `make hive-deploy` after `docker/.env` is filled from `docker/.env.example` |
| Code upgrade (default) | `make dev-deploy` |
| SQL migrations changed | `MIGRATE=1 make dev-deploy` |
| `docker/.env` only | `docker compose -p tapps-brain -f docker/docker-compose.hive.yaml up -d --no-deps --force-recreate tapps-brain-http` |

`docker/.env` **must** set non-empty `TAPPS_BRAIN_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` (compose enforces `TAPPS_BRAIN_STRICT=1`). Without it, `tapps-brain-http` crash-loops. Local dev: `http://127.0.0.1:8088,http://localhost:8088`. Verify with `make brain-smoke-live`. Details: `docs/guides/dev-docker-loop.md`.

## Cursor (IDE)

- **Quick pointers:** `AGENTS.md` — setup, tests, doc links. **VS Code/Cursor:** `.vscode/settings.json` (Python/Ruff/mypy, 100-char ruler), `.vscode/extensions.json` (recommended extensions), `.vscode/tasks.json` (pytest, ruff, mypy, `release-ready.sh`). **Indexing:** `.cursorignore` excludes `.venv/` and caches.
- **Project MCP config:** `.cursor/mcp.json` wires NLT MCP servers (`nlt-build`, `nlt-memory`, `nlt-project-docs`, etc.) via streamable HTTP on ports 8760–8765. Consumer repos use tapps-mcp BrainBridge — see `docs/operations/CONSUMER-REPO-BRAIN-WIRING.md`. Direct `tapps-brain` HTTP MCP at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/mcp/` is for brain development and coordinator agents.
- Ensure **PATH** includes `~/.local/bin` (uv tools). Run `make brain-healthcheck` after wiring changes.

